 "phase": "T1b: Bluetooth gamepads on the iPad and Apple TV, the Siri Remote for the menus",
 "change": "NTSDRuntime: OriginalGameControllerJoysticks, the AppKit host's GameController joystick code moved unchanged into a shared @MainActor class (first two extended gamepads found at launch with its 0.5 s wait, a 25 ms timer in common modes, stick or d-pad to the WinMM axes, A/B/X/Y to buttons 1-4). AppKit uses it (its copy removed). The iOS/tvOS host reports and samples gamepads through it (0 joysticks before). tvOS: the root controller is a GCEventViewController with controllerUserInteractionEnabled = false, so controller input reaches the game only through GameController (a gamepad's B is not also a Menu press, Menu does not background the app); the Siri Remote sampled every 25 ms as keys: a swipe as arrows, on the 2nd-generation remote its ring's sides as arrows and centre as Enter, on the 1st a click as Enter; Menu unmapped (Esc always asks to quit in this game). iOS and tvOS start the game from a run-loop block instead of a main-queue block so the launch probe can see paired controllers. ios_app.py: tvOS Info.plist declares ExtendedGamepad, DirectionalGamepad and MicroGamepad, GCSupportsMultipleMicroGamepads, GCSupportsControllerUserInteraction.",
 "review": "Independent review, round 1: defects - Menu mapped to Esc quits the app (Esc always opens the quit question; the iOS host's message box answers Yes) and tvOS delivers a gamepad's B as Menu, so B would quit mid-match; a remote press could run the 0.5 s probe; a launch-time gamepad count fragile as a remote guard; the probe inside a main-queue block cannot see controllers reported on the main queue. Reworked as recommended (GCEventViewController, remote through GameController, Menu unmapped, run-loop start). Round 2: OK; ring clicks on the 2nd-generation remote gave no arrows (fixed: DirectionalGamepad's cardinal dpad and centre button); open: an unmuted interactive start (checked, below), Menu during startup and Mac keyboard input in the tvOS simulator by hand, Menu at the root before App Store distribution.",
 "notes": "Scripted runs never probe or sample (the session passes --joysticks), so scenario results cannot change. The gate pinned native bd4a1da2 (shared sampler, AppKit, first iOS version); afterwards only NTSDiOS (which the gate does not build) and ios_app.py changed: final native 31898ebc, tools f3517b30. Existing hosts on the gate tree: all 10 scenarios equal, AppKit vs and playback, unchecked vs and Demo, emulator vs equal with frames identical; 0 crashes in 20 launches; 6 suites; phone A/B with music and sounds overlapping (load 5.51-6.17 against 5.97-6.31 s, main 10.82-10.88 against 10.80-10.94 ms, render, process, PSS, peak); Mac A/B overlapping (load 0.309-0.315 against 0.314-0.332 s). Final NTSDiOS: tvOS joystick, vs, demo equal and frames identical to AppKit (tw-t1b3); iPad joystick, vs, demo equal and identical (tw-t1b2; the later change is tvOS-only). Interactive launches without --script and with music and sounds on the iPad and Apple TV simulators reach the main menu; a sample shows the main thread in its run loop and the CoreAudio IO threads running (no deadlock from the run-loop start). Not checked: a real controller (needs one connected to the Mac for the simulator, or a device).",
